  "text": "The routing module predicts boundaries between adjacent elements through a similarity score [HNET:1:c007]. It measures cosine similarity between adjacent encoder outputs and computes boundary probabilities p_t = ½ (1 − (q_tᵀ k_{t‑1}) / ‖q_t‖‖k_{t‑1}‖) ∈ [0,1] [HNET:2.2.1:c023]. A hard boundary indicator b_t is obtained by thresholding p_t at 0.5, i.e., b_t = 𝟙_{ {p_t ≥ 0.5} } with p₁ = 1.0 by definition [HNET:2.2.1:c023].",
